     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg BID\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, please confirm that and give me a note on the clinical rationale to add to the order. I'd want that confirmation before entering a dose this far above the labeled maximum."
      }
